Replace each teal macro-cell in the upper-right pattern with the teal mask from the left control sprite.

Input structure:
- The black background contains three 4-connected foreground components.
- A left control sprite is a full rectangle of red and teal pixels.
- An upper-right pattern is a full rectangle of the main color and teal pixels, arranged as uniform macro-cells.
- A lower solid rectangle of the main color gives the final output size.

Rule:
- Compress the upper-right pattern into macro-cells, using the lower rectangle size divided by the control
  sprite size to determine the compressed pattern dimensions.
- Make an output filled with the main color.
- For each teal macro-cell, paste the control sprite's teal mask into the corresponding output block, turning
  the control sprite's red pixels into the main color.

Key insight:
- The upper-right object is not copied directly; it is a coarse stencil whose teal cells are substituted by
  the entire teal mask from the separate red/teal control sprite.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "symmetry/pattern",
  "src": "left red/teal control sprite and upper-right main/teal macro-pattern",
  "transform": "compress the upper-right pattern into uniform macro-cells; replace each teal macro-cell with the control sprite's teal mask, with red control pixels becoming the main color",
  "grid_shape": "same shape as the lower solid main-color rectangle"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  background: BLACK
  colors: RED(2) and TEAL(8) are fixed; one main color from {BLUE, GREEN, YELLOW} [observed]
  components: exactly 3 foreground 4-connected components on BLACK bg
  control:
    shape: square, 3x3 or 4x4
    fill: every pixel is RED or TEAL; teal fraction 40-60%
    role: stamp/mask defining teal pattern to paste into output
  pattern:
    shape: (macro_h * cell_h) x (macro_w * cell_w) where cell_h=cell_w in {1, 2}
    fill: every pixel is main_color or TEAL; each macro-cell is uniformly one color
    macro_grid: 2-3 rows x 3-6 cols; teal cells 25-50% of total
    role: coarse stencil selecting which output blocks get the stamp
  canvas:
    shape: (macro_h * stamp_h) x (macro_w * stamp_w) -- solid main_color rectangle
    role: defines output dimensions; must tile exactly by control size
  layout: |
    control and pattern share same top row, separated by 1 col of bg
    canvas is below both, separated by 1 row of bg
    all three embedded in the grid with bg border (>=1 cell on each side)
  output: canvas-sized grid; main_color everywhere except teal stamp pasted at each teal macro-cell position (RED pixels in stamp become main_color)

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick main_color from non-reserved palette; pick stamp_size in {3, 4}
    2. Create stamp (stamp_size x stamp_size) of RED and TEAL pixels; ensure teal fraction 40-60%
    3. Pick macro_grid dims macro_h in [2,3], macro_w in [3,6]
    4. Build selector (macro_h x macro_w boolean); set 25-50% cells to teal
